WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.898
Step 1. Open the Diagnostic Reports tab.

1.2
00:00:02.898 --> 00:00:06.605
It lists the encounter's diagnostic reports on the left,

1.3
00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:09.753
and shows the selected one on the right.

2.1
00:00:09.753 --> 00:00:12.555
Step 2. Find the report in the list.

2.2
00:00:12.555 --> 00:00:17.447
The newest report comes first, and each entry shows its status badge,

2.3
00:00:17.447 --> 00:00:20.002
such as Preliminary or Final.

3.1
00:00:20.002 --> 00:00:22.062
Step 3. Select the report.

3.2
00:00:22.062 --> 00:00:26.947
Care shows the selected report in the report card on the right.

4.1
00:00:26.947 --> 00:00:29.614
Step 4. Read the report details.

4.2
00:00:29.614 --> 00:00:33.617
Requested By shows who requested the service request,

4.3
00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:38.119
and filed by shows who created the diagnostic report.

5.1
00:00:38.119 --> 00:00:40.907
Step 5. Read the results and files.

5.2
00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:46.119
The Test Results table leaves out any result that a user removed.

6.1
00:00:46.119 --> 00:00:52.422
Step 6. See removed results. In the results menu, select View Observation History.

6.2
00:00:52.422 --> 00:00:58.458
The panel lists only removed results, each with the Entered in Error badge.
